{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For He judges.</b> In the sense of chastisements, as in ״כי בם ידין עמים״ — He chastises them with chastisements." "<b>And for His servants He will be consoled.</b> Nevertheless, He will be consoled concerning them by means of repentance. And so we find: ״ונחמתי על הרעה אשר דברתי עליהם״ (and I will be consoled concerning the evil that I spoke concerning them)." "<b>For He sees that the hand has slipped.</b> Their strength — that of Israel. <b>That the hand has slipped:</b> a parable — like one who drank and became drunk, and not from wine."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:15.524417443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}